The official application source archive is unmodified. Third-party libraries
retain their own notices in libs/ and vendor/. Official product documentation
is distributed separately in the runtime with its original MIT license.

The bundled PHP CLI 8.5.12 is built from unmodified official PHP source:
https://www.php.net/distributions/php-8.5.12.tar.xz
It is PHP-3.01 and includes the required Ubuntu 24.04 shared libraries. Original
notices remain in php/share/licenses and are also supplied in LICENSES/.
SOURCE.json records the PHP configure options and source input. Ubuntu library
sources are at https://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/; use apt-get source for the
matching source package on Ubuntu 24.04.

The environment builds libfaketime 0.9.12, separately preloaded for the
application clock. It is GPL-2.0-only; its full text is LICENSES/libfaketime.txt.
The unmodified corresponding source and build files are at:
https://github.com/wolfcw/libfaketime/archive/refs/tags/v0.9.12.tar.gz

Local additions start.sh, seed.php, php.ini and router.php configure SQLite,
initial tokens and the web server. The router restricts PHP execution to front
controllers and disables database download, replacement and optimization.
Errors are logged rather than displayed. Plugin installation is disabled.
These deployment files do not patch upstream application code.
